{
  "id": "356",
  "title": "Short of Money",
  "level": "intermediate",
  "date": "2017-09-10",
  "synopsis": "Do you know how to say that you are short of money in Chinese?",
  "audioUrl": "https://static.duchinese.net/documents/515/69b79d54c66d88452738df0045584d9c32aac0ed.mp3?1504501054",
  "series": null,
  "fullText": {
    "simplified": "手头紧\n\n    “我这几天手头紧，手机先不买了”，这里的“手头紧”是“钱不够用”的意思。\n    老王问老李借钱，老李不好意思说“不”，于是他对老王说：“我昨天买了手套，买小了，你知道是什么感觉吗？”\n    老王问：“什么感觉？”\n    老李回答：“手头紧啊！”\n    老王明白了，不再问老李借钱了。",
    "traditional": "手頭緊\n\n    “我這幾天手頭緊，手機先不買了”，這裡的“手頭緊”是“錢不夠用”的意思。\n    老王問老李借錢，老李不好意思說“不”，於是他對老王說：“我昨天買了手套，買小了，你知道是什麼感覺嗎？”\n    老王問：“什麼感覺？”\n    老李回答：“手頭緊啊！”\n    老王明白了，不再問老李借錢了。"
  },
  "sentences": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "simplified": "\n\n    ",
      "traditional": "\n\n    ",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "Short of Money"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "simplified": "“我这几天手头紧，手机先不买了”，",
      "traditional": "“我這幾天手頭緊，手機先不買了”，",
      "pinyin": "wǒ zhè jǐ tiān shǒu tóu jǐn shǒu jī xiān bù mǎi le",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "simplified": "这里的“手头紧”是“钱不够用”的意思。",
      "traditional": "這裡的“手頭緊”是“錢不夠用”的意思。",
      "pinyin": "zhè lǐ de shǒu tóu jǐn shì qián bú gòu yòng de yì si",
      "english": "“These last few days my hands have been tight, so I won't buy a mobile phone now.”"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "simplified": "\n    ",
      "traditional": "\n    ",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "Here “hands are tight” means to be “short of money”."
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "simplified": "老王问老李借钱，老李不好意思说“不”，于是他对老王说：",
      "traditional": "老王問老李借錢，老李不好意思說“不”，於是他對老王說：",
      "pinyin": "lǎo wáng wèn lǎo lǐ jiè qián lǎo lǐ bù hǎo yì si shuō bù yú shì tā duì lǎo wáng shuō",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "simplified": "“我昨天买了手套，买小了，你知道是什么感觉吗？”",
      "traditional": "“我昨天買了手套，買小了，你知道是什麼感覺嗎？”",
      "pinyin": "wǒ zuó tiān mǎi le shǒu tào mǎi xiǎo le nǐ zhī dào shì shén me gǎn jué ma",
      "english": "Lao Wang asked Lao Li to lend him money. Lao Li apologetically said “No”, and then told Lao Wang:"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "simplified": "\n    ",
      "traditional": "\n    ",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "“I bought gloves yesterday, but they were too small. Do you know what it feels like?”"
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "simplified": "老王问：“什么感觉？”",
      "traditional": "老王問：“什麼感覺？”",
      "pinyin": "lǎo wáng wèn shén me gǎn jué",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "simplified": "\n    ",
      "traditional": "\n    ",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "Lao Wang asked: “How does it feel?”"
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "simplified": "老李回答：“手头紧啊！”",
      "traditional": "老李回答：“手頭緊啊！”",
      "pinyin": "lǎo lǐ huí dá shǒu tóu jǐn a",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "simplified": "\n    ",
      "traditional": "\n    ",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "Lao Li replied: “My hands are tight!”"
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "simplified": "老王明白了，不再问老李借钱了。",
      "traditional": "老王明白了，不再問老李借錢了。",
      "pinyin": "lǎo wáng míng bai le bú zài wèn lǎo lǐ jiè qián le",
      "english": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "simplified": "",
      "traditional": "",
      "pinyin": "",
      "english": "Lao Wang understood, and didn't ask Lao Li to lend money anymore."
    }
  ],
